{"title":"What should I ask Julia Ioffe?","link":"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/941595050/0/marginalrevolution~What-should-I-ask-Julia-Ioffe.html","date":1769154233000,"content":"<p>Yes, I will be doing a Conversation with her.  She has a new and very good book out, namely <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://www.amazon.com/Motherland-Feminist-History-Revolution-Autocracy/dp/006287912X/ref=sr_1_1?crid=S9GLH9IPSQVK&amp;dib=eyJ2IjoiMSJ9.qO4IodUXqzaSW2VUO-EkCWuymuKFB8KXva9TVtIjsooD7Y_T-I5QE8Evn-7rKi06o03O83vYwls7hi8DdxbCAw.sZjK8GO7-wiJuuNUDGFLlEYPQe4tOwMcSKvK0CVP1-g&amp;dib_tag=se&amp;keywords=julia+ioffe+motherland&amp;qid=1769092819&amp;sprefix=julia+ioffe%2Caps%2C140&amp;sr=8-1\" target=\"_blank\">Motherland: A Feminist History of Modern Russia</a>.  I will focus on that topic, but she has done much else as well.  From <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Julia_Ioffe\" target=\"_blank\">Wikipedia</a>:</p>\r\n<blockquote><p>…a Russian-born American journalist. Her articles have appeared in <i><a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Washington_Post\">The Washington Post</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_New_York_Times\">The New York Times</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_New_Yorker\">The New Yorker</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Foreign_Policy_Magazine\">Foreign Policy</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Forbes\">Forbes</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bloomberg_Businessweek\">Bloomberg Businessweek</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_New_Republic\">The New Republic</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Politico\">Politico</a></i>, and <i><a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Atlantic\">The Atlantic</a></i>. Ioffe has appeared on television programs on <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/MSNBC\">MSNBC</a>, <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/CBS\">CBS</a>, <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/PBS\">PBS</a>, and other news channels as a Russia expert. She is the Washington correspondent for the website <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Puck_(media_company)\">Puck</a>.</p></blockquote>\r\n<p>And here is <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://x.com/juliaioffe?lang=en\" target=\"_blank\">Julia on Twitter</a>.  So what should I ask her?</p>\r\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://marginalrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2026/01/what-should-i-ask-julia-ioffe.html\">What should I ask Julia Ioffe?</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://marginalrevolution.com\">Marginal REVOLUTION</a>.</p>\r\n<img height=\"1\" width=\"1\" src=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/i/941595050/0/marginalrevolution\" />\r\n<div><a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/_/28/941595050/marginalrevolution\"><img height=\"20\" src=\"https://assets.feedblitz.com/i/fblike20.png\" /></a> <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/_/29/941595050/marginalrevolution,\"><img height=\"20\" src=\"https://assets.feedblitz.com/i/pinterest20.png\" /></a> <a href=\"https://feeds.fee